      },
      {
        "id": "lem-rpm-low-speed-remainders",
        "kind": "lemma",
        "domain": "mathematics",
        "title": "Explicit low-speed momentum and energy remainders",
        "statement": "Let $m,c>0$, let $0<\\delta<1$, and let $v\\in\\mathbb R^3$ have Euclidean norm satisfying $|v|/c\\le\\delta$. Put\n\n$$z:=\\frac{|v|^2}{c^2},\\qquad \\gamma:=(1-z)^{-1/2},\\qquad p:=m\\gamma v,\\qquad E:=\\gamma mc^2.$$\n\nThen\n\n$$0\\le\\gamma-1\\le\\frac{z}{2(1-\\delta^2)^{3/2}},\\qquad 0\\le\\gamma-1-\\frac z2\\le\\frac{3z^2}{8(1-\\delta^2)^{5/2}},$$\n\nand\n\n$$|p-mv|\\le\\frac{m|v|^3}{2c^2(1-\\delta^2)^{3/2}},\\qquad 0\\le E-mc^2-\\frac12m|v|^2\\le\\frac{3m|v|^4}{8c^2(1-\\delta^2)^{5/2}}.$$\n\nIf assigned SI kinematic units, $m$ is in kilograms, $c,v$ in metres per second, $p$ in kilogram metres per second and $E$ in joules. These are pointwise algebraic inequalities; they assume no equation of motion or empirical input.",
        "deps": [
          "thm-real-power-continuity-and-derivatives",
          "thm-chain-rule",
          "cor-mean-value-theorem",
          "thm-cauchy-mean-value"
        ],
        "dependency_roles": {
          "thm-real-power-continuity-and-derivatives": "mathematical-premise",
          "thm-chain-rule": "mathematical-premise",
          "cor-mean-value-theorem": "mathematical-premise",
          "thm-cauchy-mean-value": "mathematical-premise"
        },
        "provenance": {
          "statement": "ai-altered",
          "proof": "ai-altered"
        },
        "dependency_level": 0,
        "sources": {
          "references": [
            {
              "title": "OpenStax, University Physics Volume 3, complete textbook, Chapter 5",
              "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-3/pages/5-8-relativistic-momentum"
            }
          ]
        },
        "strategy": "direct"
      },
      {
        "id": "lem-rpm-low-speed-uniform-remainders",
        "kind": "lemma",
        "domain": "mathematics",
        "title": "Uniform low-speed relativistic remainders",
        "statement": "Let $C>0$, $0<\\varepsilon_*$, and $\\rho:=C^2\\varepsilon_*<1$. For $0<\\varepsilon\\le\\varepsilon_*$, $m,c>0$, and $v\\in\\mathbb R^3$ with $|v|\\le C\\sqrt{\\varepsilon}\\,c$, put $z=|v|^2/c^2$, $\\gamma=(1-z)^{-1/2}$, $p=m\\gamma v$, and $E=\\gamma mc^2$. Then $z\\le\\rho$ and\n\n$$0\\le\\gamma-1\\le\\frac{C^2\\varepsilon}{2(1-\\rho)^{3/2}},\\qquad 0\\le\\gamma-1-\\frac z2\\le\\frac{3C^4\\varepsilon^2}{8(1-\\rho)^{5/2}},$$\n\n$$|p-mv|\\le\\frac{mC^3c\\,\\varepsilon^{3/2}}{2(1-\\rho)^{3/2}},\\qquad 0\\le E-mc^2-\\frac12m|v|^2\\le\\frac{3mC^4c^2\\varepsilon^2}{8(1-\\rho)^{5/2}}.$$\n\nFor the formal coordinate-time Lagrangian densities\n\n$$\\mathcal L_c(v):=-mc^2\\sqrt{1-|v|^2/c^2},\\qquad \\mathcal L_N(v):=\\frac12m|v|^2,$$\n\none also has\n\n$$|\\mathcal L_c(v)+mc^2-\\mathcal L_N(v)|\\le\\frac{mC^4c^2\\varepsilon^2}{8(1-\\rho)^{3/2}}.$$\n\nSubtracting the constant rest-energy density $-mc^2$ changes an action on a fixed coordinate-time interval only by a path-independent constant. These are uniform algebraic estimates for the stipulated family; they assert no equation of motion or trajectory existence.",
        "deps": [
          "lem-rpm-low-speed-remainders",
          "thm-real-power-continuity-and-derivatives",
          "thm-chain-rule",
          "thm-cauchy-mean-value"
        ],
        "dependency_roles": {
          "lem-rpm-low-speed-remainders": "mathematical-premise",
          "thm-real-power-continuity-and-derivatives": "mathematical-premise",
          "thm-chain-rule": "mathematical-premise",
          "thm-cauchy-mean-value": "mathematical-premise"
        },
        "provenance": {
          "statement": "ai-altered",
          "proof": "ai-altered"
        },
        "dependency_level": 1,
        "sources": {
          "references": [
            {
              "title": "OpenStax, University Physics Volume 3, complete textbook, Chapter 5",
              "url": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-3/pages/5-8-relativistic-momentum"
            }
          ]
        },
        "strategy": "direct"
      },
      {
        "id": "lem-rpm-shell-force-ivp",
        "kind": "lemma",
        "domain": "mathematics",
        "title": "Orthogonal shell force local IVP and compact continuation",
        "statement": "Let $\\mathcal D\\subseteq\\mathbb R^8$ be an open coordinate-state domain with state $z=(x,U)\\in\\mathbb R^4\\times\\mathbb R^4$, and let $G:\\mathcal D\\to\\mathbb R^8$ be the smooth autonomous coordinate vector field of the shell-tangent force system in [[lem-rpm-shell-tangent-force-ivp]]. Let $z:(a,b)\\to\\mathcal D$ be its unique maximal solution. If $b<\\infty$ and there are $b_0\\in(a,b)$ and a compact set $K\\subset\\mathcal D$ such that $z([b_0,b))\\subseteq K$, then the solution extends beyond $b$, contradicting maximality. The analogous statement holds at a finite left endpoint. Therefore a finite maximal endpoint can occur only if the state eventually leaves every compact subset of its open coordinate-state domain.\n\nThis is a mathematical continuation criterion for the coordinate ODE. It asserts neither that a solution exists for all proper times nor that the background spacetime is geodesically complete.",
        "deps": [
          "lem-rpm-shell-tangent-force-ivp",
          "def-vector-valued-derivative-and-integral",
          "thm-componentwise-limits-and-continuity",
          "thm-continuous-implies-integrable",
          "cor-vector-valued-ftc-and-lipschitz-bound",
          "thm-norm-inequality-for-the-vector-valued-integral"
        ],
        "dependency_roles": {
          "lem-rpm-shell-tangent-force-ivp": "mathematical-premise",
          "def-vector-valued-derivative-and-integral": "mathematical-premise",
          "thm-componentwise-limits-and-continuity": "mathematical-premise",
          "thm-continuous-implies-integrable": "mathematical-premise",
          "cor-vector-valued-ftc-and-lipschitz-bound": "mathematical-premise",
          "thm-norm-inequality-for-the-vector-valued-integral": "mathematical-premise"
        },
        "provenance": {
          "statement": "ai-altered",
          "proof": "ai-altered"
        },
        "dependency_level": 2,
        "sources": {
          "references": [
            {
              "title": "Gautam Iyer, Brief Notes on Introduction to Differential Equations, complete ODE notes",
              "url": "https://www.math.cmu.edu/~gautam/c/2026-632/notes/existence.html"
            }
          ]
        },
        "strategy": "direct"
      },
      {
        "id": "pthm-rpm-prescribed-em-nr-trajectory-limit",
        "kind": "physics-theorem",
        "domain": "physics",
        "title": "Controlled prescribed-field trajectory limit",
        "statement": "Fix a reference speed $c_*>0$, mass $m>0$, charge $q\\in\\mathbb R$, cutoff $0<\\delta<1$, finite time $T>0$, an open time interval $I\\supseteq[0,T]$, and an open spatial region $\\Omega\\subseteq\\mathbb R^3$. In a fixed inertial chart with $x^0=ct$, let $\\mathbf E,\\mathbf B:I\\times\\Omega\\to\\mathbb R^3$ be prescribed jointly $C^1$ fields in SI units, with $\\mathbf E$ in volts per metre and $\\mathbf B$ in teslas. The same fields, mass, and charge are held fixed in the following formal family of model equations indexed by $c>0$; no Maxwell equations or empirical premise are added.\n\nChoose reference scales $L_*>0$ metres and $P_*>0$ kilogram metres per second and define the dimensionless state norm\n\n$$\\|(x,p)\\|_*:=\\frac{|x|}{L_*}+\\frac{|p|}{P_*}.$$\n\nLet $K\\subseteq\\Omega\\times\\mathbb R^3$ be compact and convex, let $P_{\\max}:=\\sup_{(x,p)\\in K}|p|$, $E_{\\max}:=\\sup_{(t,x)\\in[0,T]\\times\\pi_xK}|\\mathbf E(t,x)|$, and $B_{\\max}:=\\sup_{(t,x)\\in[0,T]\\times\\pi_xK}|\\mathbf B(t,x)|$. These field suprema are finite by the $C^1$ hypothesis on a compact cylinder. Set\n\n$$B_*:=\\frac{P_{\\max}}{mL_*}+\\frac{|q|}{P_*}\\left(E_{\\max}+\\frac{P_{\\max}B_{\\max}}m\\right).$$\n\nFor $c\\ge P_{\\max}/(m\\delta)$, define the momentum-to-velocity map\n\n$$V_c(p):=\\frac{p}{m\\sqrt{1+|p|^2/(m^2c^2)}}.$$\n\nThis is the velocity obtained from the massive mass shell and inverse momentum formula of [[pthm-rpm-inverse-momentum-and-work]]. Define the relativistic and Newtonian vector fields on $[0,T]\\times K$ by\n\n$$G_c(t,x,p):=\\bigl(V_c(p),\\,q[\\mathbf E(t,x)+V_c(p)\\times\\mathbf B(t,x)]\\bigr),\\qquad G_N(t,x,p):=\\bigl(p/m,\\,q[\\mathbf E(t,x)+(p/m)\\times\\mathbf B(t,x)]\\bigr).$$\n\nSuppose $G_N(t,\\cdot)$ is Lipschitz on $K$ with constant $L\\ge0$ in $\\|\\cdot\\|_*$, where $L$ has units $\\mathrm{s}^{-1}$. For every $c$ in the family, $G_c$ and $G_N$ are bounded by $B_*$ in $\\|\\cdot\\|_*$ on $[0,T]\\times K$, since $|V_c(p)|\\le P_{\\max}/m$. For each $c\\ge P_{\\max}/(m\\delta)$, let $J\\subseteq I$ be an open interval containing $[0,T]$ and let $x_c\\in C^2(J,\\Omega)$ satisfy $|\\dot x_c(t)|<c$. The curve $X_c(t)=(ct,x_c(t))$ is a future-timelike massive worldline with proper time $d\\tau/dt=\\sqrt{1-|\\dot x_c|^2/c^2}$, four-velocity $U_c=\\gamma_c(c,\\dot x_c)$, and $p_c=m\\gamma_c\\dot x_c$. Assume $X_c$ satisfies the adopted covariant Lorentz coupling in the prescribed field. Define $z_c(t):=(x_c(t),p_c(t))$. Let $(x_N,p_N)$ be a $C^1$ solution on $[0,T]$ of $\\dot z=G_N(t,z)$ and set $z_N(t):=(x_N(t),p_N(t))$. Require $z_c(0)=z_N(0)$ and both coordinate-state trajectories to remain in $K$. Then the relativistic coordinates satisfy $\\dot z_c=G_c(t,z_c)$, and, with $\\epsilon_c:=(c_*/c)^2$ and\n\n$$C_*:=\\frac{P_{\\max}^3}{2m^3c_*^2}\\left(\\frac1{L_*}+\\frac{|q|B_{\\max}}{P_*}\\right),$$\n\none has\n\n$$\\sup_{0\\le t\\le T}\\|(x_c(t),p_c(t))-(x_N(t),p_N(t))\\|_*\\le C_*\\epsilon_c T e^{LT}.$$\n\nHere $C_*$ has units $\\mathrm{s}^{-1}$. Consequently the state difference is $O(c^{-2})$ on this fixed interval as $c\\to\\infty$, provided the common containment and Lipschitz hypotheses hold for the family.\n\nFor every $t\\in[0,T]$, the relativistic speed satisfies $|v_c(t)|/c\\le\\delta$. If $\\mathcal E_c(t):=\\sqrt{m^2c^4+c^2|p_c(t)|^2}$ is the particle energy from the same mass shell, then [[lem-rpm-low-speed-remainders]] also gives\n\n$$|p_c-mv_c|\\le\\frac{m|v_c|^3}{2c^2(1-\\delta^2)^{3/2}},\\qquad 0\\le\\mathcal E_c-mc^2-\\frac12m|v_c|^2\\le\\frac{3m|v_c|^4}{8c^2(1-\\delta^2)^{5/2}}.$$\n\nThe limit is a formal comparison between model equations; it does not state that the SI value of $c$ varies in nature.",
        "deps": [
          "def-rpm-mechanical-momentum-and-observer-energy",
          "post-sr-massive-particle-dynamics",
          "post-em-minkowski-physical-model",
          "post-em-lorentz-coupling",
          "def-em-electromagnetic-tensor",
          "def-em-fields",
          "def-em-sources",
          "def-em-si-conventions",
          "def-em-lab-geometry",
          "def-em-relativistic-worldlines-frames",
          "pthm-em-relativistic-lorentz-force",
          "pthm-rpm-inverse-momentum-and-work",
          "lem-rpm-finite-time-ode-comparison",
          "lem-rpm-low-speed-remainders",
          "def-cross-product-in-r3",
          "thm-real-power-continuity-and-derivatives",
          "thm-chain-rule",
          "cor-mean-value-theorem"
        ],
        "dependency_roles": {
          "def-rpm-mechanical-momentum-and-observer-energy": "formulation-prerequisite",
          "post-sr-massive-particle-dynamics": "physical-assumption",
